# H3 (run 3 of 3): the HANG SHAPES at eight seats on the -u1 arm c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate-u1 (audits off, the lever on). U1 changes the trace's collective sequence (128 reduce-scatters per forward where the split ran 256, the semaphore cycling stays even),
# and the hang class was collective sequencing after long sampler-free phases, so it is gated like every new collective shape. The shapes: concurrent4_steady, concurrent8_steady, steady_resend (an engine build after many packed rounds), replay_concurrent4 and
# replay_concurrent8 (a rows=2 sequential replay), the exactness reference concurrent8_code_equal, then the split-block and drain shapes. Each run follows its own all-four reset. READ: three CONSECUTIVE completions (H1 to H3), every user at budget,
# c2_smoke_check clean (engaged line, no fall-back, two quad markers, a both-quads round), no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, the concurrent8_code_equal hashes equal in every run and equal to S0c's. A stall waits for the job timeout and records nothing, which is itself the finding.
# Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule: one stall stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/u1 development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/u1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/u1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate-u1
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,replay_concurrent8,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
